From aaac71e45e33c2d39c32ade80c0b9f568323e9b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 10:18:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] hotelops: add visible toast feedback to Load Sample /
 Reset / Relay buttons

All three buttons were already functionally correct -- verified via
Puppeteer that Load Sample Data, Reset Saved Data, and Relay to
Strategist all execute without error and Relay genuinely writes real
data to TSM_HOTELOPS_STRATEGIST_RELAY (confirmed the strategist page
renders it). The reported 'doesn't work' was very likely this: the war
room auto-loads sample data on first visit (loadFromStorage() falls
back to loadSampleData() when storage is empty), so clicking Load
Sample or Reset afterward reloads the identical data with zero visible
change on screen. And Relay had no confirmation at all -- it silently
succeeds with no on-page signal that anything happened. Both look
exactly like a broken button even though the underlying logic works.

Fix: added a toast component (matches this page's existing
amber/dark visual language) and wired a one-line confirmation into
all three handlers. Verified live: all three now show a visible toast
with the correct message, zero page errors, and relay data still
lands in localStorage as before.
